    "https://jobs.wright.edu/postings/22641": {
      "title": "Assistant Director, Campus Recreation-Facilities",
      "description": "WSU - Applicant Portal | Assistant Director, Campus Recreation-Facilities Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Assistant Director, Campus Recreation-Facilities Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Information Position Information (Default Section) EEO Statement Wright State University is an equal opportunity employer. Faculty Rank or Job Title Assistant Director, Campus Recreation-Facilities Job Category: Administrative (exempt/non-exempt) Department Student Union EEO number: 26P361 Position FTE 100% Minimum Annual Salary $50,000 Salary Band: S04 Job Summary/Basic Function: The Assistant Director for Recreation Facilities provides strategic leadership and operational management for approximately 60,000 square feet of campus recreation facilities located within the Student Union, designated recreation spaces in the Ervin J. Nutter Center, and outdoor recreation facilities. The position is responsible for long-range facility planning, operational budgeting, risk management, customer service, membership services, facility scheduling, equipment lifecycle management, and the daily operation of recreation facilities that support student engagement, health, and well-being. The Assistant Director represents Campus Recreation on university committees and collaborates across divisions to ensure recreation facilities support institutional priorities and provide an exceptional campus experience. Minimum Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in Recreation, Sports Administration, Physical Education, Higher Education Administration, Business Administration, Facility Management, or a closely related field. Minimum of three years of progressively responsible professional experience in recreation, fitness, athletics, student union, or comparable facility management. Demonstrated experience supervising, training, and developing student employees, part-time staff, or volunteers. Experience managing daily facility operations, including scheduling, customer service, facility access, and risk management. Experience using recreation management, membership, or point-of-sale software (such as Fusion or comparable systems). Experience developing and implementing policies, procedures, and standard operating practices. Strong organizational, communication, interpersonal, and customer service skills with the ability to build collaborative relationships across multiple departments. Preferred Qualifications Master’s degree in Recreation, Sports Administration, Higher Education, Business Administration, or a closely related field. Experience administering Fusion recreation management software, including membership management, reporting, and payment integration. Experience overseeing fitness centers, aquatic facilities, outdoor recreation spaces, or multi-use athletic facilities. Experience managing facility renovation, capital replacement, or equipment lifecycle planning. Experience developing risk management plans and emergency response procedures. Working knowledge of applicable safety standards, ADA accessibility requirements, and university policies. Experience with Fusion member management software. Essential Functions and percent of time: 1. Provide strategic and operational leadership for approximately 60,000 square feet of indoor and outdoor recreation facilities (including but not limited to the fitness center, gymnasium, swimming pool, locker rooms, pickleball courts). Develop long-range operational plans and facility improvement priorities; establish, implement, and evaluate departmental policies, procedures, and risk management practices; oversee daily operations; and ensure facilities support the strategic goals of Campus Recreation and the Division of Student Affairs. (35%) 2. Hire, train, schedule, supervise, and develop approximately 40 student employees providing facility coverage and customer service. (20%) 3. Manage recreation membership services including membership sales, eligibility verification, access control, point-of-sale operations, reporting, and administration of the Fusion recreation management software. Serve as the departmental expert for Fusion configuration, user accounts, program setup, payment integration, data integrity, reporting, troubleshooting, and staff training. Utilize operational and membership data to improve customer service, resource allocation, facility utilization, and operational efficiency. (15%) 4. Develop, administer, and monitor the operating budget for recreation facility operations, including equipment replacement, maintenance, memberships, facility operations, and related expenditures. Exercise independent authority for approved operational expenditures, monitor budget performance, and recommend future funding priorities that support departmental strategic objectives. (10%) Essential Functions and percent of time (cont'd): 5. Represent Campus Recreation on university committees, planning groups, and collaborative initiatives related to recreation facilities, capital improvements, facility scheduling, accessibility, safety, and operational planning. Serve as the primary liaison between Campus Recreation and campus partners including Athletics, Facilities Management, Environmental Health and Safety, Information Technology, Student Affairs, academic departments, and community organizations regarding recreation facility operations. (5%) 6. Develop and administer a comprehensive capital replacement strategy for recreation equipment, furnishings, and facility improvements, including lifecycle planning, prioritization of capital needs, and recommendations for future investments. (5%) 7. Collect, analyze, interpret, and present operational, financial, membership, participation, and facility utilization data to support strategic planning, resource allocation, assessment, and continuous improvement. (5%) Non-Essential Functions and percent of time: 8. Other duties as assigned by the Associate Dean of Campus Recreation and Sports. (5%) Working Conditions Generally an office environment with evening and weekend work required. Wright State University is an equal opportunity/affirmative action employer. To preserve the safety and security of the campus community and to maintain the integrity of university operations, it is the policy of Wright State University making an employment offer contingent on various background checks, such as a criminal record, credit history when job related and/or education verifications. Additionally, an administrative review shall be conducted whenever the university learns that an employee is charged with or convicted of a crime (except for minor vehicle violations). Frequently asked questions related to background checks may be found on the Human resources website at http://www.wright.edu/human-resources . Effective July 1, 2017, per Policy 7230 Wright State University is tobacco-free. Tobacco use, including the sale, advertising sampling and distribution of tobacco products and tobacco related items is prohibited in all university facilities, on all university owned or leased grounds, university owned or operated residence halls and apartments, and at all university sponsored events regardless of location. Tobacco use is also prohibited in all university vehicles or on any equipment owned, leased or operated by Wright State University. This policy applies to anyone on campus including students, faculty, staff, visitors, consultants, vendors, patients, volunteers, and contractor employees. Special Instructions to Applicants Posting Date 08/07/2026 First Consideration Date: 08/31/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have Bachelor's degree in Recreation, Sports Administration, Physical Education, Higher Education Administration, Business Administration, Facility Management, or a closely related field? Yes No * Do you have a minimum of three years of progressively responsible professional experience in recreation, fitness, athletics, student union, or comparable facility management? Yes No * Do you have experience planning and leading a variety of fitness activities? Yes No * Do you have any fitness certifications? (i.e. ACSM, ACE, or AFAA) Yes No * Do you have experience managing daily facility operations, including scheduling, customer service, facility access, and risk management? Yes No * Do you have experience using recreation management, membership, or point-of-sale software (such as Fusion or comparable systems)? Yes No Required Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter Optional Documents Home 3640 Colonel Glenn Hwy., Dayton, OH 45435 USA To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
