      "title": "Position Information",
      "description": "WSU - Applicant Portal | Endocrinology-Academic/General or General - Premier Physician Network Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Endocrinology-Academic/General or General - Premier Physician Network Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Please see Special Instructions for more details. This position is a Premier Physician Network  position. Please apply at: https://www.premierhealth.com/healthcare-professionals/careers/physician-jobs/opportunities/job-posting/endocrinology Position Information Position Information (Default Section) EEO Statement Premier Health and Wright State University are equal employment opportunity employers. Faculty Rank or Job Title Endocrinology-Academic/General or General - Premier Physician Network Job Category: Faculty/Instructional Department School of Medicine Admin EEO number: 26PN001 Position FTE 100% Minimum Annual Salary Salary Band: Job Summary/Basic Function: This position is a Premier Physician Network position. Wright State University and Premier Physician Network have entered into an enhanced affiliation agreement that will transform health care delivery in the Miami Valley and beyond. As part of this transformative collaboration, Wright State’s Boonshoft School of Medicine and Premier Physician Network are seeking physicians with a demonstrated ability to enhance and elevate academic health organizations in their mission of clinical care, research, and education. Together, we seek dynamic individuals with a comprehensive understanding of our mission of developing and overseeing innovative health care delivery models, sustaining excellence in clinical care, supporting academic endeavors and promoting and advancing research initiatives and scholarly activity. Outstanding strategic communication and diplomacy skills are critical as Wright State and Premier Physician Network continue to transform the health of the region in new and innovative ways. Minimum Qualifications Board Certified in Internal Medicine Completed Endocrinology Fellowship US Citizen or Permanent Residence Status Preferred Qualifications Essential Functions and percent of time: Excellent opportunities for a BC/BE fellowship-trained Endocrinologist interested in either an academic and general endocrine position or general endocrine position. The academic position includes approximately 80% patient care and 20% teaching and research. The generalist position includes 100% patient care in an Internal Medicine clinic. Essential Functions and percent of time (cont'd): Non-Essential Functions and percent of time: Working Conditions This position is a Premier Health Network position. Please apply at: https://www.premierhealth.com/healthcare-professionals/careers/physician-jobs/opportunities/job-posting/endocrinology Special Instructions to Applicants This position is a Premier Physician Network  position. Please apply at: https://www.premierhealth.com/healthcare-professionals/careers/physician-jobs/opportunities/job-posting/endocrinology Posting Date 10/14/2025 First Consideration Date: Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Required Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Home 3640 Colonel Glenn Hwy., Dayton, OH 45435 USA To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.wright.edu/postings/22501": {
      "title": "Assistant Vice President for Alumni and Donor Engagement",
      "description": "WSU - Applicant Portal | Assistant Vice President for Alumni and Donor Engagement Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Assistant Vice President for Alumni and Donor Engagement Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Information Position Information (Default Section) EEO Statement Wright State University is an equal opportunity employer. Faculty Rank or Job Title Assistant Vice President for Alumni and Donor Engagement Job Category: Department VP-University Advancement Admin EEO number: 26P303 Position FTE 100% Minimum Annual Salary Negotiable Salary Band: UC S09 Job Summary/Basic Function: By exercising a passion for connecting and building networks between donors, alumni, students, and the University, the Assistant Vice President for Alumni & Donor Engagement will set a strategic direction for the Office of Alumni and Donor Engagement by establishing goals and metrics, evaluating advancement programs and practices, and leading, coaching, mentoring, and developing a team of staff in alumni engagement, donor relations, advancement research and annual giving. The AVP will also serve as the executive director of the WSU Alumni Association. Minimum Qualifications A bachelor’s degree and five years of experience in alumni relations or university fundraising at a similar institution. • Success in cultivating and closing major gifts. • Experience in developing diverse and impactful volunteer boards. • Success in working with multi-disciplinary teams. Preferred Qualifications • A master’s degree. • Experience with working in a complex, dynamic environment connecting the philanthropic interests and needs of students, faculty, staff, and alumni with donors. • Proven ability to manage in challenging times, with multiple and diverse interests of many groups, and willingness to connect to the community. • Ability to serve as the bridge between the University and alumni/donors while advancing and protecting the interests of both. • Experience with being accountable to multiple constituents such as alumni, donors, volunteers, senior university leadership, and academic colleagues. • Superb communications skills with the ability to speak passionately about the university, our students, vision, and future. Essential Functions and percent of time: Essential function : Alumni Engagement 50% • The Assistant Vice President serves as a member of the university advancement leadership team, participating in planning processes, developing divisional goals, budgeting, and improving efficiency. Will plan, organize, and implement, in consultation with the Vice President for University Advancement, the expansion of a comprehensive and unified program of alumni engagement. • Through interaction in private and public settings, develops and nurtures relationships with key influencers in the WSU family including the president of the university, members of boards, alumni leaders, faculty, parents, students, and friends. • Leads metrics-driven strategies to continuously increase engagement of alumni and friends in alumni networks, chapters, events, volunteer roles, and fundraising. • Provides strategic direction for the Alumni Engagement team and the Alumni Association Board of Directors. • Ensures each programmatic area of their portfolio has clearly outlined goals, operating plans, and measures of success that are tracked in a way that shows growth and depth of engagement. • Ensures that volunteers and their respective leadership structures, are representative of the breath of the alumni population, have strong succession planning, and are aligned with the strategic direction of the WSU Alumni Association. • Demonstrates mature judgement, impeccable integrity and excellent skills to establish an environment of confidentiality and will handle sensitive matters in a discreet manner. • Represents the university and the alumni association professionally both internally and externally. Essential Functions and percent of time (cont'd): Essential function : Leadership & Program Management 25% • Builds a cohesive team of professionals who are inspired to collaborate in new and innovative ways to support and ensure the success of WSU’s engagement and campaign efforts. • Creates protocol and procedures that ensure the continuity of service delivery to our alumni and donors across our team. • Establishes policies, standard operating procedures, goals, metrics and other key performance indicators to measure the ongoing effectiveness of the programs under their leadership. • Creates and leads an innovative outreach effort that accelerates growth in alumni and donor volunteerism and engagement within their scope of responsibility. • Collaborates across all areas of the Advancement team to provide leadership and opportunities for shared growth in programs and engagement. • Develops and maintains relationships with key volunteer leadership across the university. • Leads, mentors, and inspires new and existing staff members through a combination of transparency, effective communication, and modeling of collaborative behavior. • Manages the budgets for each area of responsibility. Manages the daily work of the alumni engagement, donor relations, advancement research, and annual giving teams. This includes deploying staff and budgeted financial resources to achieve specified goals and objectives. Essential function : Philanthropy 25% • Participates as part of WSU’s leadership team for the next campaign, which will focus on scholarships and student success. • Maintains a portfolio of alumni major gift prospects. • Partners with the AVP for Corporate Relations to identify opportunities for corporate and affinity partnerships. • Partners with major gifts team to ensure a healthy pipeline of engaged donors. • Provides strong leadership and support to the Annual Giving team to ensure resources are in place for continued growth. • Shares the WSU story with a variety of constituencies while being a presence at university events. Provides strong leadership for staff in planning effective alumni and campaign events. Non-Essential Functions and percent of time: Working Conditions Regular office environment. Will work weekend and evening events throughout the semester. Travel for Alumni Events in and outside of Ohio will be expected. To preserve the safety and security of the campus community and to maintain the integrity of university operations, it is the policy of Wright State University making an employment offer contingent on various background checks, such as a criminal record, credit history when job related and/or education verifications. Additionally, an administrative review shall be conducted whenever the university learns that an employee is charged with or convicted of a crime (except for minor vehicle violations). Frequently asked questions related to background checks may be found on the Human resources website at http://www.wright.edu/human-resources . Effective July 1, 2017, per Policy 7230 Wright State University is tobacco-free.  Tobacco use, including the sale, advertising sampling and distribution of tobacco products and tobacco related items is prohibited in all university facilities, on all university owned or leased grounds, university owned or operated residence halls and apartments, and at all university sponsored events regardless of location. Tobacco use is also prohibited in all university vehicles or on any equipment owned, leased or operated by Wright State University.  This policy applies to anyone on campus including students, faculty, staff, visitors, consultants, vendors, patients, volunteers, and contractor employees. Special Instructions to Applicants Posting Date 06/15/2026 First Consideration Date: 07/01/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this position at Wright State University? Please check all that apply. WSU Careers website Academic Careers Academic Keys Chronicle Diversity in Higher Ed Diverse Issues in Higher Ed Facebook HBCU Higher Ed Jobs Inside Higher Ed LinkedIn Social Media Personal referral Women in Higher Ed Other Job Fair or Hiring Event Required Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter References Optional Documents Home 3640 Colonel Glenn Hwy., Dayton, OH 45435 USA To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.wright.edu/postings/22424": {
      "title": "Male Teaching Associate (Part-time on call) (General Announcement)",
      "description": "WSU - Applicant Portal | Male Teaching Associate (Part-time on call) (General Announcement) Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Male Teaching Associate (Part-time on call) (General Announcement) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Information Position Information (Default Section) EEO Statement Wright State University is an equal opportunity employer. Faculty Rank or Job Title Male Teaching Associate (Part-time on call) (General Announcement) Job Category: Administrative (exempt/non-exempt) Department Medical Education-BSOM EEO number: 27H039 Position FTE PTOC Minimum Hourly Rate $36.29/hr. Salary Band: UC HR7 Job Summary/Basic Function: Male Teaching Associate ( MTA ) – To provide instruction to medical students and other health related personnel, on procedures for conducting a basic, accurate and comfortable clinical genital-rectal male exam. Minimum Qualifications Applicants must have a high school diploma or GED and must be age of 18 or over. Must be comfortable in dealing with varying student populations and personalities. Applicant must have self-control, be sensitive and have strong concern for men’s health issues. Applicant must demonstrate exceptional interpersonal and teaching abilities. Familiarity with medical environment and role-playing are helpful. Preferred Qualifications Essential Functions and percent of time: 40% MTA will instruct medical students and other health related personnel on the procedures for conducting a basic, accurate and comfortable clinical genital-rectal male exam. 30% MTA will participate as teacher, trainer, proctor and actual patient when working with medical students and other health related personnel. 30% MTA will instruct the students in learning appropriate communication, technical, clinical and patient education skills. Essential Functions and percent of time (cont'd): Non-Essential Functions and percent of time: Working Conditions Professional clinical setting in exam or conference rooms. To preserve the safety and security of the campus community and to maintain the integrity of university operations, it is the policy of Wright State University before making an employment offer conduct various background checks, such as a criminal record, credit history when job related and/or education verifications. Additionally, an administrative review shall be conducted whenever the university learns that an employee is charged with or convicted of a crime (except for minor vehicle violations). Frequently asked questions related to background checks may be found on the Human resources website at http://www.wright.edu/human-resources. Effective July 1, 2017, per Policy 7230 Wright State University is tobacco-free. Tobacco use, including the sale, advertising sampling and distribution of tobacco products and tobacco related items is prohibited in all university facilities, on all university owned or leased grounds, university owned or operated residence halls and apartments, and at all university sponsored events regardless of location. Tobacco use is also prohibited in all university vehicles or on any equipment owned, leased or operated by Wright State University. This policy applies to anyone on campus including students, faculty, staff, visitors, consultants, vendors, patients, volunteers, and contractor employees. Special Instructions to Applicants Posting Date 05/27/2026 First Consideration Date: Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a high school diploma or GED? Yes No * Do you meet the age requirement of this position? Yes No * How did you hear about this position at Wright State University? Please check all that apply. WSU Careers website Academic Careers Academic Keys Chronicle Diversity in Higher Ed Diverse Issues in Higher Ed Facebook HBCU Higher Ed Jobs Inside